Generated by `scripts/inline-shapes/gen_sha256_shape.py`; do not edit by hand.

Each `chunkN_eq` says that chunk `N` of the generated rows (100 rows) is a run of the
blocks of `Sha256.Rows`, and Lean checks it by `rfl`. A round that a chunk boundary cuts
appears as `(roundRows b n).take k` at the end of one chunk and `(roundRows b n).drop k`
at the start of the next. `sha256RowsAutoList_eq` and `sha256InitRowsAutoList_eq`
assemble the chunks. A single `rfl` on all rows exceeds the default recursion depth, as
for the frame checks of `FrameInstances`.
-/

